:: story.opening.new-home -> @exit
  @auto enter-place
  @place-key player_home
  @when not flags.home.opening_seen
  @priority 1000
  @heading "A new beginning"
  @choices "How do you feel about the day ahead?"

  @passage wake-up

  Pale morning light falls across a room filled with cardboard boxes. Most of your clothes are still packed, the kitchen contains almost nothing, and the key to your new home is lying beside the mattress.

  You moved in yesterday. Today is supposed to be your first proper day in the city.

  Your phone vibrates against the floor. The school has sent you another reminder: your first class begins at 09:00. If you intend to arrive on time, you should get moving soon.

  @choice "Maybe this is a fresh start" -> .get-moving
    @effect set local.outlook "hopeful"
  @endchoice

  @choice "I already hate this place" -> .get-moving
    @effect set local.outlook "resentful"
  @endchoice

  @choice "Just get through today" -> .get-moving
    @effect set local.outlook "guarded"
  @endchoice

  @passage get-moving

  @if local.outlook == "hopeful"
    A new home, a new school, and a city where nobody knows you yet. Perhaps that can be a good thing.
  @elseif local.outlook == "resentful"
    New walls and a different school do not make this feel like home. For now, getting through the day will have to be enough.
  @else
    You push the unopened boxes from your mind. One thing at a time: get ready, find the school, and make it through the day.
  @endif

  [info]Your phone is always available from the Phone button or by pressing P. Reminders tracks obligations such as school, while GPS lists known destinations and can guide you through the city. Opening the phone does not advance time.[/info]

  School is waiting, but what you do next is your decision. You can get ready, leave immediately, or ignore it and spend the day another way.

  @choice "Get up" -> @exit
    @effect set flags.home.opening_seen
  @endchoice

  @#==============================================================================================

:: place.player-home
  @hub player_home

  @if not story.home.unpacking or story.home.unpacking < 2
    You are back in the privacy of your four walls. Cardboard boxes crowd the little open floor space, and most of the flat still feels borrowed rather than lived in.
  @elseif story.home.unpacking < 5
    You are back in the privacy of your four walls. The bathroom is usable now, though unopened boxes still line the walls.
  @elseif story.home.unpacking < 10
    You are back in the privacy of your four walls. Your clothes are put away and the table is clear, giving the flat the beginnings of a routine.
  @elseif story.home.unpacking < 15
    You are back in the privacy of your four walls. With the bed properly assembled, the bedroom finally looks like somewhere you can recover at the end of the day.
  @elseif story.home.unpacking < 20
    You are back in the privacy of your four walls. Most of the flat is ready for company; only a stubborn cluster of boxes remains.
  @else
    You are back in the privacy of your four walls. Everything has found a place, apart from the strange receptacle uncovered beside the wall.
  @endif

  @if not flags.home.computer_unpacked and flags.inventory.computer
    A computer is still packed in a box on the floor. You can unpack it to set it up on the desk.
  @elseif flags.home.computer_unpacked
    A shiny brand new computer gives your room a certain je-ne-sais-quoi. You feel like a rich person!
  @endif

  @choicegroup "Bedroom"

    @choice "Go to Bed" -> menu.player.home.rest
      @hint energy 1 "++Energy"
    @endchoice

    @choice "Lift weights" -> @exit
      @time 5m
      @when not daily.home.weightlifting and story.home.unpacking >= 10
      @change skill strength 0.1
      @effect set daily.home.weightlifting
    @endchoice

    @choice "Sit down with your diary" -> home.diary
      @when story.home.unpacking >= 5
    @endchoice

    @choice "Closet" -> home.clothes
      @when story.home.unpacking >= 5
    @endchoice

  @endchoicegroup

  @choicegroup "Activities"

    @choice "Unpack" -> home.unpack
      @when not story.home.unpacking or story.home.unpacking < 19
      @time 15m..30m
      @effect add story.home.unpacking 1
    @endchoice

    @choice "Unpack the last boxes" -> home.unpack.receptacle
      @when story.home.unpacking == 19
      @time 15m..30m
      @effect add story.home.unpacking 1
      @effect set flags.quest.receptacles.started
      @effect set flags.home.unpacked
    @endchoice

    @choice "Unpack your computer" -> @exit
      @when flags.inventory.computer and not flags.home.computer_unpacked
      @response
        You unpack your computer and set it up on the desk. The screen flickers to life, and you can now use it to browse the web, check your email, and play games.
      @endresponse
      @time 15m
      @effect set flags.home.computer_unpacked

    @endchoice

  @endchoicegroup

  @choicegroup "Bathroom"

    @choice "Take a shower" -> @exit
      @when story.home.unpacking >= 2
      @time 15m
      @change stat hygiene +50
      @change stat energy -5
    @endchoice

    @choice "Brush your teeth" -> @exit
      @when story.home.unpacking >= 2
      @time 5m
      @change stat hygiene +5
    @endchoice

  @endchoicegroup

  @choicegroup ""
    @choice "Examine the strange receptacle" -> home.receptacle
      @when flags.quest.receptacles.started
    @endchoice
  @endchoicegroup

:: home.unpack -> @exit

  @if story.home.unpacking < 5
    You open another box and sort its contents into rough piles. The room is still crowded, but there is a little more space to move.
  @elseif story.home.unpacking < 15
    Another armful of belongings finds a proper place. Bit by bit, the anonymous rooms are beginning to look like yours.
  @else
    You flatten more cardboard and deal with the awkward things you kept putting off. Only a few boxes remain now.
  @endif

  @if story.home.unpacking == 2
    You empty the bathroom boxes, stack your toiletries by the sink, and clear enough clutter to use the shower without climbing over anything. Now you can get clean - about time, too.
  @elseif story.home.unpacking == 5
    You finish sorting your clothes and clear the table beneath the window. There is finally somewhere to sit, think, and write.
  @elseif story.home.unpacking == 10
    The pieces of the bed frame emerge from behind a wall of cardboard. Once it is assembled and the mattress is lifted into place, the bedroom immediately feels more comfortable.
    Hey, that box has some of your knicknacks too! You put the weights in the bedroom and the small decorations on the shelves. The flat is starting to feel like home.
  @elseif story.home.unpacking == 15
    You arrange the remaining furniture and make room for another person to sit. The flat is no longer too embarrassing to invite someone into.
  @endif

  @next -> @exit

:: home.unpack.receptacle -> @exit
  After you put away the final box, you notice a strange receptacle wrapped in a dusty material. Its surface is cool and seamless, with no obvious way to open it.
  It reminds you of the strange plinths in that movie you watched... the space one.

  @next

  You try moving it, to no avail. It's either heavy or bolted to the floor. You wonder if it is some kind of puzzle, or if it is just a decorative piece. Either way, you have no idea what to do with it.

  @next

  Guess you'll just have to live with your new roommate for now. You trash the final cartboard box and take a moment to admire the newly cleared space. The flat is finally starting to feel like home.

  @next -> @exit

:: home.clothes -> @exit

  Your clothes are sorted and within easy reach. Once the clothing system is in place, this is where you will be able to choose what to wear.

  @next -> @exit

:: home.diary -> @exit
  @heading "Diary"
  @system journal.diary

:: home.receptacle -> @exit

  You press your hands to the receptacle thingy, but cannot find a seam, switch, or recognizable marking. Whatever it is, unpacking has only raised a new question.

  @next -> @exit

:: menu.player.home.rest -> @exit
  @passage rest-menu
  @choicegroup "Set your alarm to:"

    You set your alarm and climb into bed. The soft sheets and warm blankets are a welcome comfort.
    @if not story.home.unpacking or story.home.unpacking < 10
      For now, the mattress is still on the floor and the unopened bedroom boxes make the space feel cramped.
    @else
      With the bed assembled and the bedroom cleared, settling down is noticeably easier.
    @endif
    How long will you sleep for?

    @choice "8 hours" -> .wake-up
      @time 8h rest
      @effect stat hygiene -5
    @endchoice

    @choice "7 hours" -> .wake-up
      @time 7h rest
      @effect stat hygiene -4.5
    @endchoice

    @choice "6 hours" -> .wake-up
      @time 6h rest
      @effect stat hygiene -4
    @endchoice

    @choice "5 hours" -> .wake-up
      @time 5h rest
      @effect stat hygiene -3.5
    @endchoice

    @choice "4 hours" -> .wake-up
      @time 4h rest
      @effect stat hygiene -3
    @endchoice

    @choice "3 hours" -> .wake-up
      @time 3h rest
      @effect stat hygiene -2.5
    @endchoice

    @choice "2 hours" -> .wake-up
      @time 2h rest
      @effect stat hygiene -2
    @endchoice

    @choice "1 hour" -> .wake-up
      @time 1h rest
      @effect stat hygiene -1.5
    @endchoice

  @endchoicegroup

  @next "Leave" -> @exit

  @passage wake-up

  Your alarm goes off.
  @if player.energy >= 80
    You feel well-rested, and you quickly shake off the last remnants of sleepiness.
  @elseif player.energy >= 50
    You feel a little groggy, but you manage to get out of bed.
  @else
    You feel exhausted, and you wish you'd slept longer. You drag yourself out of bed and get ready for the day.
  @endif

  @next -> @exit
